Package: lcos-desktop-config
Version: 1.1.0-2
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: 484
Maintainer: LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>
Homepage: https://lunduke.com
Depends: lcos-branding (>= 0.7), lcos-theme-clearlooks (>= 0.7), lcos-settings (>= 1.1.0-1), lunduke-terminal
Replaces: libgarcon-common, xfce4-panel, xfce4-helpers, xfce4-settings
Recommends: elementary-xfce-icon-theme, gtk2-engines
Description: LCOS XFCE defaults (xdg, skel, wallpaper, menus)
 System and skel XFCE look: xfconf XML, panel default.xml, helpers.rc,
 applications menu, wallpaper first-login seed (no overwrite), Hidden stock
 helper .desktop overrides, Science directory hide, and Lunduke
 Terminal as the XFCE terminal helper. Games uses the lunduke-city package's
 desktop file for Lunduke City; this package only hides stock Micropolis
 if needed (usr/local/share/applications/micropolis.desktop).
 .
 0.9.5-1: lid close suspends on AC and battery without locking (xfpm
 lid-action-on-ac/-battery=1; stock was lock screen, #143).
 .
 0.9.5-2: tap-to-click on by default for touchpads
 (/etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/50-lcos-touchpad.conf: libinput Tapping and
 TappingDrag on; libinput's default is off).
 .
 0.9.5-3: Brave Origin is the Xfce web browser again: ships
 /usr/local/share/xfce4/helpers/brave.desktop, the stock brave helper with
 brave-origin and brave-origin-stable added to X-XFCE-Binaries (the stock
 one finds no brave binary, so links opened a browser chooser); and
 /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list defaults x-scheme-handler/http and https to
 brave-origin.desktop.
 .
 0.9.6-1: /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list defaults Debian packages
 (application/vnd.debian.binary-package, alias application/x-deb) to
 gdebi.desktop, so double-clicking a downloaded .deb opens GDebi to
 install it instead of Xarchiver; Xarchiver keeps every other archive
 type. GDebi itself comes from lcos-base 0.9.6-3 (Depends gdebi).
 Editor 2026-10-23.
 .
 0.9.6-2: Thunar's "Open Terminal Here" opens Cool Retro Term in that
 folder instead of the home folder (#166). The Cool Retro Term
 TerminalEmulator helper now runs /usr/bin/lcos-cool-retro-term, which
 starts cool-retro-term with --workdir set to the directory it was
 launched in (cool-retro-term ignores its starting directory without it).
 .
 0.9.6-3: a custom wallpaper survives reboots. lcos-set-wallpaper (login
 autostart) treated a monitor with no top-level last-image as new and
 stamped its workspace0 with the stock wallpaper, centered, on every
 login; xfdesktop 4.20 keeps the user's choice only under
 workspaceN/last-image, so the choice was wiped at each reboot. It now
 exits at once after the first seeded login, skips any monitor whose
 workspaces hold a non-stock image, and stamps workspace0 only when it
 has no image yet. The stock default style is now zoomed (image-style 5)
 instead of centered (1) in /etc/xdg and skel xfce4-desktop.xml and in
 the script. Editor 2026-10-23.
 .
 1.0.1-2: one workspace by default (no virtual desktops). xfwm4
 /general/workspace_count is 1 and /general/workspace_names is a single
 entry ("Workspace 1"), in /etc/xdg and skel, and in the includes.chroot
 copies. Alt+Insert (add workspace) and Alt+Delete (delete workspace)
 are unbound: xfce4-keyboard-shortcuts.xml in /etc/xdg/lcos and skel
 sets /xfwm4/custom/override and a full copy of the libxfce4ui 4.20.1
 xfwm4 shortcuts, with those two commands empty. Other shortcuts stay
 the stock ones. Editor 2026-11-09.
 .
 1.1.0-1: version bump for LCOS 1.1.0. No functional changes.
 Editor 2026-11-12.
 .
 1.1.0-2: Lunduke Terminal replaces Cool Retro Term. helpers.rc
 TerminalEmulator=lunduke-terminal, the panel launcher is
 org.lunduke.LundukeTerminal.desktop, and the Cool Retro Term helper
 and lcos-cool-retro-term wrapper are gone. On upgrade, a home
 helpers.rc changes only the line TerminalEmulator=cool-retro-term;
 any other terminal choice is kept. A panel launcher is replaced only
 when its only Exec is cool-retro-term, and only if every such launcher
 is still that command. Thunar Open Terminal Here stays
 exo-open --working-directory %f --launch TerminalEmulator; Lunduke
 Terminal honors that directory. Depends on lcos-settings and
 lunduke-terminal, so an upgrade configures the terminal alternative
 before this package pins it. The Settings
 menu opens Command Center. Covered XFCE settings dialogs are hidden
 with NoDisplay files in /usr/local/share/applications. postinst diverts
 /usr/bin/xfce4-display-settings to the Command Center hot-plug wrapper
 and removes that diversion on purge.
 Editor 2026-11-12.
 .
 Live-only installer bits are not included.
